codex
The failure is caused by this audit sandbox hiding `/proc/self/exe`; Lean 4.22’s runtime consequently cannot locate its own application, even though the pinned binaries and libraries are present. I’ll use a narrowly scoped local interposer that answers only `readlink("/proc/self/exe")` with the process’s own absolute `argv[0]`; all other filesystem calls remain unchanged. I’ll preserve the source, hash, and probe results, then rerun the unmodified trusted preflight. This restores executable-location discovery and does not alter the generated project or Lean’s theorem checking.
